592186417701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417699 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417701 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417701 1077 "selection" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417701 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417692 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417701 1079 #uuid "2afbf87d-1c06-55f7-9a1b-f8b6764e8f1d" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417685 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417691 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417693 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417696 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417698 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1077 "selection" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417696 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417702 1079 #uuid "4b17b4e5-ae42-5c71-8493-ac975ab35b5e" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417701 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1069 "q-38893" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1071 "Which of the following statements are true given that $T:{R}^{5}\\to {R}^{5}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and $T(x)=v$ has no solution? \n\n- $T$ is invertible\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n- $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1072 #uuid "0464e7a7-ce22-55cd-90ec-4b6a71a12079" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417703 1074 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{5}$ into ${R}^{5},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=5 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $T(x)=v$ has no solution, we have that $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T),$ hence $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{5}.$ According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{5},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that  $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417702 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1069 "q-84053" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T$ and ${u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\in {R}^{3}.$  Consider the following statement:\n\n*If ${u}_{1}-{u}_{2}\\ne 0$ and $T({u}_{1})-T({u}_{2})=0,$ then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3$\n- $T$ is invertible" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1072 #uuid "c77aeb41-578d-533f-87d1-e33216f35c1e" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417704 1074 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $T$ is a linear transformation and $T({u}_{1})-T({u}_{2})=0,$ we have $T({u}_{1}-{u}_{2})=0.$ So ${u}_{1}-{u}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T)$ and ${u}_{1}-{u}_{2}\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we must have $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$, then $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3,$ the transformation $T$ can't be invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417705 1062 #uuid "291db6d3-4728-529e-a9be-f15ca20db25d" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417705 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417704 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417706 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417705 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417706 1062 #uuid "3efa04eb-3c5c-549f-ac5a-28d6ca38cb8b" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417706 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125164 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417707 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417706 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417707 1062 #uuid "8823976c-e582-552f-a786-db586ba8c928" 13194139534288 17592186045417 true] [17592186417707 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417703 13194139534288 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-a321f5ff-d1ce-5778-90d0-3e0d34ad246d" 17592186417684 "answer-2f10238c-7d05-58b9-96e8-9c69a8801161" 17592186417685 "answer-64373e5d-5dd7-5b8c-997e-b1a1d51821a3" 17592186417686 "answer-6bdc2284-27e4-5704-8274-3bbae725fe40" 17592186417687 "answer-7ed9e009-1eed-587e-99c2-a5c90a12f34a" 17592186417688 "answer-86137dd0-1a5b-577a-bcd9-2df89f80ba0f" 17592186417689 "answer-8ba47e3f-5df2-5d3d-9f48-fd9b4dac64f8" 17592186417690 "answer-b1eb1104-92b0-5dcf-bd12-07d9a0132bf5" 17592186417691 "answer-bd086813-aae0-5b88-80fb-38d4e70fa634" 17592186417692 "answer-d5329d0a-dafa-5056-a8ca-478564ecacb5" 17592186417693 "answer-e41cc51f-809d-5496-8f87-309d33b65dcd" 17592186417694 "answer-eb